    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a balanced slate today, but the optimizer is heavily favoring the middle-infield and leadoff spots. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads the squad with a 74.39 efficiency score, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Fisher and a prime #4 spot in the order. He is joined at the top of our priority list by **Drake Baldwin** (70.84), whose position atop the lineup against Eduardo Rodriguez provides a massive 10% order bonus, pairing nicely with his strong xwOBA metrics. **Jacob Wilson** also provides a high-floor start (63.95) despite facing a tougher southpaw in MacKenzie Gore, as he capitalizes on a significant park factor boost.\n\nWe are navigating a few \"Lineup Pending\" designations that inject volatility into today\u2019s projections. The most difficult benching decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the cut at 48.30. While he offers intriguing upside, the optimizer preferred the stability of **Luis Lara** in the final OF slot and **Liam Hicks** at catcher; **Nasim Nunez** was ultimately squeezed out due to a negative park factor and unfavorable SP skill metrics against Sean Manaea. Meanwhile, we remain cautious with our elite bats: **Kyle Tucker** (54.04) and **Andy Pages** (50.86) face the toughest arm on the board in Jacob Misiorowski (2.03 xERA). While we are starting them, the severe SP skill penalty (-19%) highlights that these are \"start-on-talent\" plays rather than matchup exploits. Furthermore, **Gunnar Henderson** (43.19) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (39.89) are relegated to the bench today, as the combination of tough opposing pitching and negative platoon splits makes them risks for our daily caps.",
